Estimate the number of tokens French-learning children hear per month. Estimates were retrieved from Le Normand & Thai-Van (2022). Table 1 includes the number of children in each age group and the group mean of word tokens heard in a session, which were 20 minutes long
```{r}
# Estimate the weighted mean of tokens per session
group_means <- c(127, 199, 256, 392, 414, 486, 494, 491, 475)
group_sizes <- c(39, 32, 38, 36, 37, 34, 33, 35, 31)

mean_tokens_per_session <-  weighted.mean(group_means, group_sizes)

# Estimate tokens per month
mean_tokens_per_month <- round(mean_tokens_per_session * 3 * # Tokens per hour, given that sessions were ~20 minutes long
                                                  12 * # Tokens per day, assuming each child hears 12 hrs of child-directed speech per day
                                                  30.44, # Token per month, with 30.44 days in an average month
                              digits = 0)
```
The number of monthly tokens heard by French-acquiring children is not very different from the monthly tokens for English-acquiring children (438336). And given that our sample is North American, the English tokens will be used for French models.

Retrieve French data from CHILDES
```{r Read CHILDES data}
## Retrieve data from Braginsky et al (2019)
load("data/uni_joined.Rdata") # This data frame includes all words in all languages. Includes word frequency measures from CHILDES

# Estimate tokens per month in French
# 183 nouns
fre_tokens_per_month <- uni_joined %>% 
  filter(language == "French (Quebec)", # Keep only French Tokens
         measure == "produces") %>% # Keep word production data only, as comprehension was included
  select(uni_lemma, lexical_classes, words, word_count) %>% 
  rename(fre_item = words,
         lexical_class = lexical_classes) %>% 
  group_by(fre_item) %>% 
  filter(row_number() == 1, # Keep only one row per type
         !is.na(word_count)) %>% # Remove types that do not have word count (they were not on CHILDES?)
  ungroup() %>% 
  # The following line are based on Kachergis_etal_2022/get_childes_freqs
  mutate(prob = word_count / sum(word_count), # Estimate the probability that a word is heard
         tok_per_mo = prob * 438336, # Multiply the probability of each word times the number of tokens a child hears on average in a month. This is the same number of monthly tokens used for English
         lexical_class = case_when(str_detect(lexical_class, "nouns") ~ "nouns",
                                   TRUE ~ lexical_class), # Set lexical class to "nouns" those cells that contain "nouns", even if they also include other lexical class
         # Change the spelling of some items so they match the spelling from Wordbank
         fre_item = case_when(fre_item == "divan" ~ "divan/sofa",
                              fre_item == "nouilles/pâtes, spaghetti" ~ "nouilles/pâtes",
                              fre_item == "ourson/nounours, toutou" ~ "ourson/nounours",
                              fre_item == "toast/rôtie" ~ "toast",
                              fre_item == "pantalon" ~ "pantalons",
                              fre_item == "brosse à dent" ~ "brosse à dents",
                              fre_item == "parc (d´enfant)" ~ "parc (d'enfant)",
                              TRUE ~ fre_item)
  )

save(fre_tokens_per_month, file = "data/fre_tokens_per_month.RDS")
```

